# Read by ripgrep in addition to VCS ignore files, and — unlike them — still
# honoured under `--no-ignore-vcs`, which ripgreprc turns on globally. That
# split is the point: VCS ignore hides whole nested repos from a search rooted
# above them, while these are directories nobody ever wants to read.
#
# Generic entries only. Anything true of one workspace or repo belongs in its
# own `.ignore`, which ripgrep reads from ancestors of the search path.

node_modules/

# Worktree checkouts are excluded per repo instead, in that repo's own .ignore:
# a multi-component pattern here does not match from above a repo root, while a
# basename one broad enough to work would hide directories nobody meant to hide.
.venv/
__pycache__/
dist/
build/
.next/
.nuxt/
.turbo/
.svelte-kit/
coverage/
.vercel/
*.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
